{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And I fell down before HaShem as at the first, forty days.</b> The sense of ואתנפל is that he would fall to the ground before Him, for here the Rabbis of blessed memory derived the order of prayer that they instituted for us in three modes, and they are sitting, standing, and falling: sitting, as it is written ״ואשב בהר״ and so on; standing, as it is written ״ואנכי עמדתי בהר״; falling, as it is written ״ואתנפל לפני ה׳״." "<b>And in the Midrash</b> to Tehillim, at the verse (Psalms 90:1) ״תפלה למשה״ — 'A prayer of Moshe' — Rabbi Berakhiah says: Moshe left no corner of the firmament upon which he did not pray, as it is said: ״ואתנפל לפני ה׳״." "<b>By way of the Kabbalah:</b> ״ואתנפל לפני ה׳״ — there were two prayers. He says that he prayed to the specific Name forty days and forty nights, and he did not mention what the prayer was; and the expression he does mention — ״על כל חטאתכם אשר חטאתם לעשות הרע בעיני ה׳ להכעיסו״ — explains that what they did with the calf and their severing of the covenant angered by this the specific Name. And when he says further on ״ואתפלל אל ה׳ ואומר אדני אלהים אל תשחת״, he prayed to the attribute of Judgment and he did mention what the prayer was, and that is the very prayer that he mentioned in Ki Tissa (Exodus 32:11): ״למה ה׳ יחרה אפך בעמך״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:47:07.592588556Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}